---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PhysicalClusterTopology from "../../utils/distributed/PhysicalClusterTopology.astro";

// Deterministic pseudo-random noise so the page is stable between builds.
let seed = 5;
const rand = () => {
	seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 2 ** 32;
	return seed / 2 ** 32;
};
// GPU temperatures (°C), with one hot server.
const temps = Array.from({ length: 48 }, (_, g) => 62 + rand() * 8 + (Math.floor(g / 4) === 7 ? 14 : 0));
---

<Layout title="PhysicalClusterTopology demo">
	<h1>PhysicalClusterTopology demo</h1>
	<p>
		The three-tier network MegaScale describes (§3.4): every GPU has its own NIC, NIC <em>i</em> of every server is
		wired to ToR switch <em>i</em> of its pod ("multi-rail"), ToRs connect to every spine in the pod, and spine
		<em>s</em> of every pod connects to core <em>s</em>. Hover or click a GPU to colour every other GPU by how many
		switches its traffic would cross.
	</p>

	<h2>12 servers of 4 GPUs, pods of 3</h2>
	<PhysicalClusterTopology servers={12} gpusPerServer={4} serversPerPod={3} spinesPerPod={4} selected={20} />

	<h2>With per-GPU values</h2>
	<PhysicalClusterTopology
		servers={12}
		gpusPerServer={4}
		serversPerPod={3}
		spinesPerPod={4}
		values={temps}
		colors="inferno"
		unit="°C"
		valueLabel="GPU temperature"
		distanceColors="greens"
	/>

	<h2>8-GPU servers</h2>
	<PhysicalClusterTopology servers={8} gpusPerServer={8} serversPerPod={4} spinesPerPod={4} nicGbps={400} />
</Layout>
